<section class="pt-12 pb-8">
  <h1 class="section-title">Workflow</h1>
  <p class="section-lede">
    From blank board to first beat in about ten minutes.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">1. Record a sample</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
    Press and hold <span class="badge">REC</span>, tap a step button
    (1–8 for drum slots, 9–16 for melodic slots on RavinePhoenix —
    these ranges are swapped vs. a stock PO-33; see ADR-0002), and the
    firmware starts capturing mic input into that slot's PSRAM region.
    Release <span class="badge">REC</span> to stop.
  </p>
  <div class="terminal">
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> rec 0
    <span class="text-slate-400"># records into slot 0 (drum)</span><br>
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> stoprec
    <span class="text-slate-400"># stops; sample is finalized in PSRAM</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">2. Trim and slice</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
    Each slot has a start and end point. Select the slot with
    <span class="badge">SOUND</span> + a step pad, then move the
    start/end markers in Tweak Trim mode (tap
    <span class="badge">FX</span> until it reads TRIM, then Knob A =
    start, Knob B = end), or send raw commands over UART.
    (<span class="badge">SOUND</span> + step <em>selects</em> a slot; it
    does not move the trim markers.)
  </p>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
    Drum loops can be auto-sliced into 16 equal parts; melodic slots
    play as a single sample with chromatic pitch shifting.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">3. Sequence</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
    Press <span class="badge">WRITE</span> to enter write mode, select a
    sound (<span class="badge">SOUND</span> + step), then press step pads
    to place it on those steps. Press
    <span class="badge">PLAY</span> to start the sequencer. The 2.4″ TFT
    shows the playhead.
  </p>
  <div class="terminal">
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> bpm 140<br>
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> pattern 0<br>
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> play<br>
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> status<br>
    <span class="text-slate-400">seq: playing bpm=140 step=4 pattern=0</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">4. Apply punch-in FX</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
    Hold <span class="badge">FX</span>, then press one of the 15 effect
    pads (pad 16 = "no effect"). The active effect name shows on the
    TFT. Some highlights:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-1">
    <li><strong>Loop 16/12/Short/Shorter</strong> — different loop lengths</li>
    <li><strong>Octave Up/Down</strong> — pitch shift by ±12 semitones</li>
    <li><strong>Stutter 4/3</strong> — granular repeat</li>
    <li><strong>Reverse</strong> — plays the slot backwards</li>
    <li><strong>Bitcrush</strong> — 4-bit downsample distortion</li>
    <li><strong>Filter Sweep</strong> — automated low-pass cutoff</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">5. Save patterns + samples</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
    Patterns are saved to flash via the LittleFS partition. Samples
    stay in PSRAM and reload after a reboot.
  </p>
  <div class="terminal">
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> save
    <span class="text-slate-400"># writes patterns + per-slot sample blobs</span><br>
    <span class="text-po33-300">po33&gt;</span> load
    <span class="text-slate-400"># reloads from flash</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">6. Sync &amp; chain</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
    Pulse OUT fires on every 16th note for syncing with other Pocket
    Operators or analog gear. Use the shell to chain patterns into
    full songs (up to 128 patterns in sequence).
  </p>
</section>